## 2. Layered Architecture Implementation

FoodieHub strictly adheres to the clean 4-tier layered architecture:

```
[ HTTP Requests ]
       │
       ▼
[ Routes Layer ]         (routes/*.js: strictly route declarations & middleware binding)
       │
       ▼
[ Middlewares Layer ]    (auth.js, rbac.js, validate.js, rateLimiter.js, errorHandler.js)
       │
       ▼
[ Controllers Layer ]    (controllers/*.js: req/res mapping & HTTP status codes)
       │
       ▼
[ Services Layer ]       (services/*.js: 100% pure business logic, calculations, rules)
       │
       ▼
[ Data Access Layer ]    (models/*.js: Mongoose models, indexes, bcrypt hooks)
       │
       ▼
[ MongoDB Database ]     (mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/foodiehub)
```

No business logic is placed in route files. Every public method is decorated with JSDoc comments. Responses follow the uniform `{ success, message, data, error }` contract.

